=== Techniques ===
The extinguishing operation employed several techniques:

* '''Water cooling:''' Firefighters used high-pressure [[water]] jets to cool the wellheads and surrounding equipment, reducing temperatures enough to allow approach.
* '''Explosive snuffing:''' [[Explosive charges]] were used to "snuff out" fires by momentarily removing [[oxygen]] from the combustion zone. This technique was particularly effective for high-pressure wells.
* '''Dry chemical extinguishing:''' [[Dry chemical]] agents (primarily [[sodium bicarbonate]] and [[potassium bicarbonate]]) were used to smother smaller fires.
* '''Heavy equipment:''' [[Bulldozer|Bulldozers]] and [[Excavator|excavators]] were used to remove damaged equipment and prepare wellheads for capping.

The operation was complicated by the presence of [[Land mine|land mines]] and [[unexploded ordnance]] left by retreating Potocsino forces. Military [[Combat engineer|combat engineers]] had to clear each well site before firefighters could approach.

